_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the retry-budget and fuse thresholds are configurable (config surface) vs. intentionally fixed constants, and justify the choice.","cohort":["T12","T2","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.818,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'At most three physical invocations and 15 seconds cumulative sleep per logical postcondition'","'opens after three consecutive exhausted eligible logical outcomes across at least two tickets. Provider scope additionally requires two endpoint families.'","ABSENCE: no statement that these thresholds are config-driven rather than hardcoded constants"],"finding":"The numeric policy thresholds (three physical invocations, 15s cumulative sleep, ~2s/4s fallback delays, three consecutive exhausted outcomes, two-ticket / two-family fuse gates) are asserted as fixed values with no statement of whether they are configurable; these are exactly the kind of operational thresholds expected to evolve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb881b5ab8e94c82d","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved policy section","norm_id":"n489ca8cc1a8396b4","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operators need to tune the fuse sensitivity or retry budget for a slow tenant without a code change","A provider's Retry-After routinely exceeds 15s and the budget needs adjustment"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a line to Approved policy declaring these values as named, configurable defaults (with the current numbers as defaults) or explicitly justify why they are fixed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate"